# Environment variables per environment

- **MacBook / local dev (this Cursor workspace):** use **`.env.local`** at the repo root (gitignored). Set `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` and other keys the app reads at build or runtime. Restart `npm run dev` after changes so Next.js reloads env.
- **Production / staging:** set the same logical keys on the host (Vercel, the SSH deploy target, etc.) or in GitHub Actions secrets—never commit real values to tracked files.
- **Documentation:** keep **`.env.example`** updated with every required or optional variable name and a one-line comment; local secrets stay only in `.env.local` or the deploy UI.
- When helping debug “missing config,” say whether the fix belongs **on the Mac in `.env.local`** vs **in the deploy provider’s env UI**.
